1
00:02:30,031 --> 00:02:35,771
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:36,051 --> 00:02:40,051
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:40,311 --> 00:02:44,251
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:44,851 --> 00:02:49,131
Bucky D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum-gum fruit,

5
00:02:49,411 --> 00:02:51,891
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:52,271 --> 00:02:54,851
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:55,171 --> 00:02:57,991
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:57,991 --> 00:03:01,051
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:02,391 --> 00:03:03,791
This is exciting!

10
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:07,631
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:08,371 --> 00:03:11,411
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:11,631 --> 00:03:15,671
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:21,051 --> 00:03:25,971
After being separated from his crew, Luffy set out to rescue his captured brother, Ace.

14
00:03:25,971 --> 00:03:29,431
To do so, he snuck into the government prison, Impel Down.

15
00:03:31,051 --> 00:03:36,191
Together with Captain Buggy, as well as former Baroque Works agents, Mr. Three and Bonclay,

16
00:03:36,631 --> 00:03:40,231
Luffy was able to make his way to level four, the Burning Heat Helm.

17
00:03:40,231 --> 00:03:47,231
But as soon as he arrived, he was poisoned by Magellan, the Warden of Impel Down,

18
00:03:47,451 --> 00:03:48,631
and taken into custody.

19
00:03:55,391 --> 00:03:58,831
After Luffy was imprisoned on level five, the Freezing Hell,

20
00:03:59,251 --> 00:04:02,431
Bonclay did everything in his power to find a way to save him.

21
00:04:02,431 --> 00:04:04,931
No freaking way!

22
00:04:05,711 --> 00:04:08,771
I mean, uh, what do you mean you can't make an antidote?

23
00:04:08,971 --> 00:04:09,871
What's the hold-up?

24
00:04:11,171 --> 00:04:12,091
A miracle?

25
00:04:12,731 --> 00:04:13,031
Huh?

26
00:04:13,331 --> 00:04:14,191
Oh, yeah!

27
00:04:14,471 --> 00:04:15,831
I forgot about him!

28
00:04:16,051 --> 00:04:17,231
He's in Impel Down!

29
00:04:17,571 --> 00:04:18,351
My hero!

30
00:04:18,631 --> 00:04:19,731
The miracle worker!

31
00:04:20,071 --> 00:04:20,731
Come on!

32
00:04:20,871 --> 00:04:22,771
We need to find out where they're holding him now!

33
00:04:22,771 --> 00:04:28,251
A paradise in hell!

34
00:04:28,591 --> 00:04:30,931
Impel Down level 5.5!

35
00:04:35,071 --> 00:04:35,971
Uh-oh.

36
00:04:36,331 --> 00:04:37,491
I think we're surrounded.

37
00:04:46,011 --> 00:04:48,191
Well then, we have no choice.

38
00:04:48,291 --> 00:04:49,831
We should lock ourselves inside.

39
00:04:49,831 --> 00:04:54,311
Right, I'll try to distract the mutts.

40
00:04:54,531 --> 00:04:55,171
Make it quick!

41
00:04:57,171 --> 00:04:58,291
Chew or miss!

42
00:04:58,471 --> 00:04:59,871
My special muggy ball!

43
00:05:00,971 --> 00:05:02,211
Good riddance!

44
00:05:04,291 --> 00:05:06,291
What the hell?!

45
00:05:06,291 --> 00:05:09,651
Now I've done it!

46
00:05:10,651 --> 00:05:11,931
Yeah, you did?

47
00:05:13,611 --> 00:05:15,671
Yep, I broke the key!

48
00:05:17,051 --> 00:05:18,471
Why are you so useless?

49
00:05:19,831 --> 00:05:23,031
Crap, it's too late!

50
00:05:24,531 --> 00:05:25,671
Take this!

51
00:05:25,871 --> 00:05:26,491
Candles!

52
00:05:26,591 --> 00:05:27,071
No!

53
00:05:35,171 --> 00:05:36,651
That was close.

54
00:05:36,831 --> 00:05:37,811
Come on, move!

55
00:05:38,071 --> 00:05:39,711
Let's make a run for the cell pronto!

56
00:05:39,711 --> 00:05:42,751
I don't think that we'll need to.

57
00:05:43,471 --> 00:05:44,911
I just had an idea.

58
00:05:48,171 --> 00:05:49,151
Stupid wolf!

59
00:05:49,431 --> 00:05:51,751
Try and eat us now, you frozen fleabags!

60
00:05:52,591 --> 00:05:55,691
It's no use trying to bite your way through, Mr. Wolf.

61
00:05:55,951 --> 00:05:57,911
This candle house is as hard as iron.

62
00:05:58,251 --> 00:06:00,451
Even with fangs so big and powerful as yours,

63
00:06:00,551 --> 00:06:02,051
there's no way you'll break it!

64
00:06:02,051 --> 00:06:02,891
You said it!

65
00:06:02,891 --> 00:06:03,711
Let's head out!

66
00:06:04,091 --> 00:06:05,311
But of course, my friend!

67
00:06:07,211 --> 00:06:08,591
One, two!

68
00:06:09,291 --> 00:06:10,891
One, two!

69
00:06:11,051 --> 00:06:12,211
Maybe you're not useless!

70
00:06:12,511 --> 00:06:14,831
I'm so happy right now, I'll take that as a compliment!

71
00:06:15,831 --> 00:06:17,131
One, two!

72
00:06:17,131 --> 00:06:23,311
